-- Still-all &\ (ruled 2026-07-11): the column intact up to here — one latch along the march order. Trips off at the first false and stays off. Twin of s63-still-all.bqn.
-- A column of six soldiers marching. &\ is the boolean scan of &: each position answers "all alive so far?", the complement latch of s62.
-- Decoy 0s sit behind !MarchOrder (rows 2, 6): an early 0 in the out is a selection leak; length 6 = popcount of the order pins the same-length invariant. The order is index order (the 16-scans convention).
--! registry ../registries/s63-still-all.reg

--! out 1 1 1 0 0 0
&\ Alive @ MarchOrder
